{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/965620-damaging-spells-and-explosions","id":965620,"title":"Damaging spells and Explosions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T05:50:28-07:00","id":965620,"title":"Damaging spells and Explosions","content":"Let's say I want to take a spell like Celestial Fire, and instead of targeting 1 person with the full effect of heavenly fire I want to use it like a grenade from the Hurt Locker. Can I do that? How do I do that? After all explosions have 3 primary factors. Damage the amount of force suffered by someone at the epicenter of the blast, the primary target of the blast. Then there is force, the damage applied to everyone else. Blast radius the is number of yards for the primary force of the blast, the total distance is equal to double that amount.<br /> <br /> So Umm...First my own theory. Converting any spell to a blast first costs 1 mana. Why? Because I feel that helps balance things.<br /> So damage and Force let's start with those. Those are derived from potency. Divide potency equally by these any remainder goes into force.<br /> <br /> Blast radius = the number of steps in scale.<br /> <br /> So is this a good method? What do you all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:43:15-07:00","id":965668,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that requires it to cost Mana. Just cast the spell on an area instead of a single target. The downside is that you hit <i>everything</i> in the area. Turning an already Wisdom-risking attack spell into a dangerous area-of-effect is a price unto itself. You also reduce your dice pool a bit to target an area, reducing the potential damage you could inflict.<br /> <br /> In other words, yeah, you can do this, and no, you don't need to worry about it too much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:48:25-07:00","id":965674,"title":"","content":"Use Advanced Scale for maximum fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T09:05:21-07:00","id":965710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/965620-damaging-spells-and-explosions?p=965668#post965668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing that requires it to cost Mana. Just cast the spell on an area instead of a single target. The downside is that you hit <i>everything</i> in the area. Turning an already Wisdom-risking attack spell into a dangerous area-of-effect is a price unto itself. You also reduce your dice pool a bit to target an area, reducing the potential damage you could inflict.<br /> <br /> In other words, yeah, you can do this, and no, you don't need to worry about it too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you use the version of advanced scale that targets a number of individuals instead? Also, how'd you handle the Wisdom part of this on the table (trying to learn some stuff before finally running a game!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T09:35:12-07:00","id":965719,"title":"","content":"You could, depending on the number and size(s) of your targets. Different tools for different situations.<br /> <br /> As for Wisdom... Depends on the Mage. Depends on the situation. Gimme details on each and I'd be happy to offer suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:35:40-07:00","id":965738,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> Okay. Here is one I thought of.<br /> <br /> Ammon has been helping some nuns set up a mission for battered and abused women. The nuns it seem have run afoul of one of the gangs in Metcalfe Park. Ammon managed to convince them to follow him as he leads them away from the sisters and their charges.<br /> <br /> He manages to lead them into an open enough area that he can see them all. These men had come to do harm, to do worse than the robbers Ammon of old faced. He still wouldn't kill them, but maiming, crippling, and in general making them repent their life choices that lead to this moment. That seemed well within his shadow name.<br /> <br /> He holds his sword and slams the tip of the blade into the ground<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> Okay dice time.<br /> What do I want to do. Make Celestial fire go off like a incindierie grenade.<br /> <br /> I'm using a path tool and shadow name (2) as Yantra<br /> <br /> Let's assume I have prime 4 and gnosis 1<br /> The potency is 4<br /> Stepping up the scale by 1<br /> <br /> Let's assume 2 reach are spent to cut casting time to instant, and the range to sense.<br /> <br /> So my casting pool is 7<br /> The damage is 2 which would effect only the guy at the center for 2a of the blast/explosion, the guys with 2 yards of him (including him) take 2l along with 2 dice of lethal, the guys at 4 yard out take 2 dice lethal.<br /> <br /> At least that is if I'm understanding the explosive damage right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:33:52-07:00","id":965767,"title":"","content":"I think we're going to have many fun discussions, Hapless.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you're designing the spell like that, though. With a damaging spell in an area, it'd affect all targets within the area equally; that is, they all take the same damage. You could make it try and use the traditional explosive rules, but that makes the spell weaker. Furthermore, without Reach and Mana, it can't inflict Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> With all the factors of the spell you've described and included, everyone inside the radius is burned for four damage (Bashing or Lethal depending on if it's Fraying or Unraveling).<br /> <br /> So, using the factors you've described, Ammon would stick his blade in the ground and smite the bastards with heavenly flame for four damage within an area the size of a small room. No hope of evasion.<br /> <br /> Given that he's acting in keeping with his Persona and acting in keeping with his Virtue (I imagine), I'd call for a Wisdom roll at Understanding (three dice) with a +2 bonus. He acted in keeping with his Virtue and the nature of his soul, but he still used magic to injure others. If he planned this out beforehand and weighed consequences, I'd give him an extra +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:48:51-07:00","id":965775,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> I look forward to it. Am I going to have to share the story of the individual my shadow name comes from to enhance understanding in the future?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:51:05-07:00","id":965777,"title":"","content":"You're welcome to, but a link would be better if it's a historical figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:05:37-07:00","id":965780,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia Article. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammon_(Book_of_Mormon_missionary\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammo...mon_missionary</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}